      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Moradol was used for postoperative analgesia in 39 patients subject to urgent surgery. Promedol was used as a control. It has been found that a marked pain syndrome in the early postoperative period in patients examined was characterized by certain deviations of the parameters studied. Moradol, as compared to promedol, has a better analgesic effect, causing milder respiration and hemodynamic changes. With intravenous drug injection, a more profound analgesia is associated with a greater respiratory depression."},
